    {
      "date": "2026-09-01",
      "entity_type": "solution",
      "path": ".cg-docs/solutions/testing-patterns/2026-09-01-verify-cross-layer-invariants-beyond-coverage.md",
      "slug": "2026-09-01-verify-cross-layer-invariants-beyond-coverage",
      "status": "",
      "summary": "The package passed 837 tests, Ruff, Pyright, and a 97.82 percent statement-plus-branch coverage gate. A light verification review still found blocking semantic failures. Examples included: - Accepted graph edges could cite evidence for a different route. - Routed variables could disagree with inventory links. - Independent conditional branches were compared as if they were one branch. - Source bindings omitted companion-file content. - Stable artifact projections could disagree with the active pointer after a hard process exit. - Exact-wheel tests did not exercise the changed routing runtime. The aggregate gates proved that code paths executed. They did not prove that...",
